      "contents": "module cit294.test\n  facts\n    ✔ unblocked MAT canary: content type retained as declared, despite the real bytes being the MAT/HDF5 payload\n    ✔ unblocked MAT canary: matload is the loader libvips actually selected\n    ✔ unblocked MAT canary: the dummy file's exact bytes and count are recoverable from the returned variant -- not just a trusted boolean\n    ✔ unblocked MAT canary: independently (via strace, outside the Ruby process) confirmed open of the dummy file\n    ✔ blocked MAT canary: no loader ran and the *actual variant call* raised the specific block error -- a generic crash does not satisfy this\n    ✔ blocked MAT canary: no disclosure field claims a match, and no returned bytes are present at all (refusal, not a silent empty read)\n    ✔ blocked MAT canary: independently (via strace) confirmed the dummy file was never opened -- not merely that the script didn't report it\n    ✔ PNG control processes normally whether or not untrusted loaders are blocked, with byte-exact pixel data in both cases\n    ✔ all four arms ran against the identical pinned image -- the verdict is about one configuration, not a drifting rebuild\n    ✔ the runtime configuration each verdict is bound to is recorded, not assumed\n    ✔ reconciling each observation against its declared claim raises no flags\n    ✔ a claim that disagrees with reality is exactly what gets flagged\n    ✔ negative control: a generic crash does not pass as a successful block, even with the blocking env var and no loader selected\n    ✔ negative control: the right error class with an unrelated message does not pass either\n    ✔ negative control: emptying the returned bytes/count is caught even though matches_dummy_file still says true\n    ✔ negative control: corrupting the blocked PNG control's pixels is caught, independent of the MAT canary's own checks\n    ✔ negative control: a deleted/zeroed independent trace for the unblocked MAT arm is caught -- this is the exact CIT-297 finding (an empty or falsified strace trace previously still passed all 28 assertions)\n    ✔ negative control: a trace falsely reporting a dummy-file read during the blocked arm is caught -- the other half of the same CIT-297 finding\n  examples\n    ✔ mat-unblocked\n    ✔ mat-blocked\n    ✔ png-unblocked\n    ✔ png-blocked\n\n100.0% tests pass [22 passed], 100.0% asserts pass [56 passed]\n"
